# shell: desktop
# DB-054/DB-058: Ctrl+Tab raises the switcher, and the strip is drawn.
note Ctrl+Tab opens it
key Tab ctrl
wait 3
expect-title Switcher
shot /tmp/trk_script/switcher.png
note its bottom edge is where a 12 px name row puts it
expect-pixel 470 344 828282
note Tab again moves on, and Escape takes it away
key Tab
wait 2
key Escape
wait 3
note now raise the interface to 16 px and ask for the strip again: the
note row that holds the picked window's NAME was written down as 22 px,
note which is what a 12 px face needs and no more
click 980 20
wait 4
menu-pick Settings
wait 4
menu-pick Fonts
wait 12
expect-title Fonts
click 652 300
wait 12
click 652 310
wait 12
expect-font Sans 16
key w ctrl
wait 8
key Tab ctrl
wait 6
expect-title Switcher
note and now the strip reaches two pixels further at each end: the icons
note are a fixed size, so all of the growth is the name row under them
expect-pixel 470 344 d8d8d8
key Escape
wait 3
quit
